  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental funds only (no proprietary funds; fiduciary funds not in trim). Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). beginning_cash/ending_cash are the cash basis fund balances the statement rolls forward (ending 31,169,098 = cash 28,397,865 + investments 2,771,233, p3); investments are inside that figure so ending_investments is left null. Proceeds from Sale of Bonds 9,853,707 is printed under other financing sources -> debt_proceeds. Taxes 14,411,762 kept unsplit: no printed breakdown by tax type (as Adams County FY2023-24). Balance sheet from the governmental funds Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances (p3), whose totals equal the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (pp5-6, departments not itemized); Road & Bridge, COVID ARP and Law Enforcement Center budget schedules (pp7-8); COVID ARP one-line disbursements 296,785 split into General Government 15,000 and Capital Outlay 281,785 from that fund's column on p4. Nonmajor funds: combining statement has 15 fund columns (pp13-16), so its Total Nonmajor Funds column is used (fund = Nonmajor funds (combined)); the per-fund nonmajor budget schedules (pp9-12, one receipts/disbursements line per fund) are not recorded to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-16 of 16 Balances are the printed \"Cash basis fund balances - beginning / ending\" rows, recorded as fund balance like this county's other years (2026-11-19)."
